# The Graveyard of the American Dream.

**Authors:** Swanson, Gordon I.

## Abstract
Criticizes the 1987 National Endowment for the Humanities report for blaming &quot;vocationalism&quot; for declining humanities enrollments in colleges. Unlike other disciplines, humanities leaders seem unwilling to seek clients or to engage in self-examination. What's needed is a renaissance of educational populism, or a repackaging of the humanities that increases their accessibility to everyone. (MLH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ370244

